      ],
      "name": "Entity tracking (OnAddEntity / OnRemoveEntity)",
      "summary": "Hook the engine's entity-system listener instead of walking dwEntityList every frame. CEntitySystem keeps a CUtlVector<IEntityListener*> at +0x30; install a small shim with two virtuals (OnAddEntity, OnRemoveEntity) and the engine will call it whenever a CEntityIdentity is bound or torn down. Cache (handle → entity*) in your own flat array and you skip ~16k pointer-chases per second versus the loop. \n\nFalls back automatically: on the first frame after attach, do one full walk to seed the cache, then run from listener events thereafter."
    },
