      "name": "FOV Changer",
      "summary": "Two-prong approach. (1) Hook the world-FOV resolver in client.dll (signature GetWorldFovResolver) and return the desired value when the local pawn is not scoped — keeps the value sticky against engine resets. (2) Every tick write the desired FOV into m_iFOV and m_iFOVStart on the camera services AND into m_iDesiredFOV on the local controller. The controller-level field is the canonical source the renderer reads; without it the camera-services side gets clobbered back to default."
